# act (nektos/act) default flags for local CI iteration.
#
# Usage: invoke `act` (or via tools/act-cell) from repo root; act reads
# this file automatically. See AGENTS.md §3.6 "Local CI iteration with
# act" for the operator-facing workflow.

# Runner image — custom `ghcr.io/elijahr/lockfree-ci:latest`, built and
# published by `.github/workflows/build-image.yml` from
# `.github/docker/lockfree-ci.Dockerfile`. Pinned for ALL ubuntu-*
# runners so act + GHA can share the same environment.
#
# The image is multi-arch (linux/amd64 + linux/arm64), so act picks the
# host architecture natively — no qemu emulation on Apple Silicon.
#
# Why custom rather than `catthehacker/ubuntu:*`:
#   - js-latest installs node via nvm; bare `docker exec cmd=[node ...]`
#     can't find node (no shell init). `actions/cache@v4` crashes with
#     `exec: "node": executable file not found in $PATH`.
#   - full-latest is ~70GB extracted (verified push 20). Pull cost and
#     disk cost are prohibitive on the operator host, and the cache
#     step STILL failed in some matrix cells.
#   - Our needs are narrow: ubuntu base + Nim (pinned via asdf) +
#     apt nodejs + git + gh + clang + valgrind. ~2-3GB image, fast pull,
#     bit-identical to what GHA jobs see when `container:` is set.
-P ubuntu-latest=ghcr.io/elijahr/lockfree-ci:latest
-P ubuntu-22.04=ghcr.io/elijahr/lockfree-ci:latest
-P ubuntu-24.04=ghcr.io/elijahr/lockfree-ci:latest

# No --container-architecture pin: the image is multi-arch, so act
# (and Docker BuildKit / containerd) pull the native variant for the
# host. On Apple Silicon this means linux/arm64 with no qemu — faster
# local iteration. On amd64 hosts (GHA-runner-like) it means linux/amd64
# natively.

# Reuse containers across runs of the same job so dep installs cache.
# Combine with `--rm` on the CLI if you want a clean slate.
--reuse

# Always check for image updates before running. ~1s overhead per
# invocation (Docker daemon HEADs the registry); in exchange, image
# updates published by build-image.yml flow into local act runs without
# manual `docker pull`. If the overhead becomes intolerable, flip back
# to `--pull=false` and refresh manually with
# `docker pull ghcr.io/elijahr/lockfree-ci:latest`.
--pull=true

# Persistent artifact/cache servers so actions/cache@v4 hits across act
# runs. Both directories live under ~/.cache/act and survive between
# invocations; the operator (or wrapper) handles cleanup. See AGENTS.md
# §3.6 "Caching" subsection.
--artifact-server-path /Users/eek/.cache/act/artifacts
--cache-server-path /Users/eek/.cache/act/cache
